 "Thin and dated polling, with one August poll showing Cuellar up 11"], "rationale": "Cuellar combines incumbency, a cash advantage, and a history of outrunning the district's Republican lean, while markets and most raters put him clearly ahead. Tijerina's fundraising and national profile keep this from being Safe, but the evidence points to a Likely Democratic hold.", "watch": "Any fresh polling showing Tijerina closing within single digits, or a major corruption-focused news cycle against Cuellar, would move this toward a Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Henry Cuellar (D) is running."]}, "overview": "South Texas's 28th District pairs a Republican-leaning electorate with one of the House's most durable Democratic incumbents. Henry Cuellar has repeatedly won here despite the district's lean, and he enters the general with a fundraising edge and more than $1.1 million on hand. His Republican challenger, Webb County Judge Tano Tijerina, is a serious recruit who has raised nearly $1.4 million and drawn national GOP attention, including appearances with Trump administration figures.\n\nRaters mostly call the race Lean or Likely Democratic, and prediction markets price Cuellar's chances near 90 percent. The only recent independent poll, from late August, showed Cuellar up 11 points, though polling here is sparse. A tepid endorsement from LUPE Votes and corruption attacks from Tijerina are the main friction points, but the overall picture favors Cuellar.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9009, "margin": 7.69}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8765, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8779, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8804, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8627, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.8617, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8973, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8968, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9013, "m